# the bitwise cyclic tag program is written using 0__, 1__, and h__ symbols,
# and the initial data using 0.. and 1.. (both with left-to-right corresponding
# to first-to-last)
# h is a halt instruction, and can be placed after a 1 in order to halt if the
# front of the data is 1
# the program will not halt until all in-progress append operations have completed,
# which allows the final data string to be read conveniently

# wikipedia gives this example of a simple meaningless 2-tag system:
# a => ccbaH
# b => cca
# c => cc
# (with H being the halt symbol)
# the program used below is a conversion of that system, with initial word baa

xxx
